.DS_Store
game/.godot/
game/build/*
!game/build/.gdignore
target/
game/reports/
# Per-run project-setting override — the ONLY way to boot this project
# windowed now that it defaults to full screen (the engine's --windowed flag
# loses to the project setting). tools/probe_visibility.sh writes it and
# removes it; a crashed run must not leave a committable stray.
game/override.cfg
# Per-session agent worktrees. Unignored, `git add -A` stages these as
# embedded-repo gitlinks with no .gitmodules — they clone as empty dirs.
.claude/
.worktrees/
# Per-plan scratch for subagent-driven development: task briefs, implementer
# reports, review packages, and the progress ledger. The skill self-ignores
# only `.superpowers/sdd/`, and only once its first script has run — so the
# window before that call, and anything ever written outside `sdd/`, are
# covered by nothing. Hence the rule for the whole directory, here.
.superpowers/
# The godot-mcp editor addon — a DEVELOPER TOOL, never a shipped dependency,
# and the one thing under game/addons/ that must never be committed.
#
# Two reasons, both load-bearing. deploy.sh ships the tree by `git archive`
# into a bare repo whose post-receive hook untars it, so anything committed
# here reaches the droplet AND the wasm export — a Node-backed debugging tool
# riding into the shipped game. And ci/vendor-gdunit4.sh governs this
# directory on the assumption that gdUnit4 is its only tenant: its `verify`
# fingerprints the tree, so a second addon is drift it would have to be taught
# to forgive.
#
# Install it locally (`npx @satelliteoflove/godot-mcp --install-addon`) and
# leave it untracked. test/repo_hygiene.sh pins both halves of that: nothing
# under the path is tracked, and this rule still covers it.
game/addons/godot_mcp/
